  "90c6afa5933232b2d366870660168d3ab5203e690b4643064278be2ea41ed80d": "Process Engineer – HVAC and industrial cooling systems Description The engineering group is responsible for the design, construction, upgrade and implementation of production, process and infrastructure systems in the plant, while meeting quality, safety and regulatory requirements. The department leads engineering projects from the characterization and planning stage, through the establishment and execution to delivery to the internal customer and validation accompaniment. Job description • Design, characterization and writing of engineering specifications for process systems and infrastructures. • Leading engineering projects from the stage of defining the requirements, planning, procurement, construction and execution until delivery to the internal customer. • Responsibility for HVAC systems, chillers, cooling towers, cold water systems, air handling units (AHU), ventilation systems and structure control. • Preparation of PFD, P&ID, CUs, characterization documents and work protocols. • Performing thermal load calculations and characterizing cooling and air conditioning requirements for facilities and process equipment. • Accompanying contractors, suppliers and consultants from the planning stage to the completion of the project. • Support of IQ/OQ/PQ processes and validation of infrastructure and process systems. • Leading change control processes and examining their impact on processes, equipment and systems. • Analyzing system performance, locating bottlenecks, troubleshooting and implementing corrective and preventive actions. • Leading projects for energy efficiency and improving reliability and systems availability. • Working with production, maintenance, quality, validation and safety departments. • Ongoing engineering support of the production and infrastructure systems on the site. • Leading improvement teams and cross-organizational projects. Education requirements • Bachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering, Chemical – Mandatory. Professional experience • At least 3-5 years of experience as a process engineer or project engineer in the industry – mandatory. • Experience in planning, setting up and running systems from the planning stage to delivery – mandatory. • Proven experience in industrial HVAC and cooling systems – mandatory. • Experience working with chillers, cooling towers, cold water systems, AHU and ventilation systems – mandatory. • Experience in a pharmaceutical, biotechnological, food or other regulatory industry – an advantage. • Experience in managing engineering projects and working with contractors and suppliers – an advantage. Professional knowledge • Understanding validation processes and GMP requirements. • Ability to read and prepare engineering drawings, P&ID and process drawings. • Knowledge of control systems and industrial equipment. • Familiarity with HVAC standards and industrial infrastructures. • Experience in performing thermal load calculations and energy analysis – an advantage. Apply for a job © Niloosoft 2026",
