  "be0585c977f1662b60d7d45468e33f2c615c60e9d52828ad9860b6c92ebe7617": "Associate Quality Product Release & QC Oversight Description of integration into the group responsible for implementing current Good Manufacturing Practices (cGMP) rules and international standards binding the enterprises in the field of pharmaceuticals. The group members carry out direct supervision of the QC laboratories and the quality control of the product. In addition, the group is responsible for reviewing and approving batch files, releasing batches in accordance with the company's procedures and regulatory requirements, managing and handling customer complaints, and more. Job Description: • Implementation and adherence to work according to procedures and GMP requirements. • Direct supervision of QC laboratories and performance of quality assurance according to cGMP procedures. • Conduct ongoing tours of the QC laboratories in order to monitor and supervise the laboratory processes. • Accompanying and handling quality records: laboratory investigations, deviations, corrective actions and change controls in the fields of laboratories. • Review and approval of batch files – Checking documentation and performing production processes and laboratory tests. • Writing policy procedures, reviewing and approving factory work procedures. • Writing periodic quality reports, preparing presentations and presenting them. • Conducting internal audits. • Investigating and managing customer complaints. • Accompanying regulatory audits. • Training employees on quality issues. Requirements • Bachelor or above in Life Sciences/ Biotechnology/Chemistry/Biochemistry/Pharmacy /Biomedical Engineering – Mandatory. • Qualifications and previous knowledge / experience: - Prior experience in the field of quality assurance, background in processes in the pharmaceutical industry, good familiarity with regulatory requirements on various cGMP issues - Experience in laboratory work (from the pharma field) and working under GMP - skills – personal responsibility, good interpersonal relations, working in a computerized environment, independence, self-study ability, task management ability, high level English - high oral and written expression ability. Apply for a job © Niloosoft 2026",
  "c3e98a1f420635edc0319b6ba6ce1e82c3d14db5f3ad39da512b800b3ed55dfe": "Student for QC Microbiology Laboratory Description The laboratory is responsible for performing microbiological tests of the company's products during the various life cycle stages including environmental monitoring tests throughout the production area. The Microbiology Laboratory is responsible for providing microbiological services of all kinds to all the factory's customers, including providing professional solutions and advice for all company activities related to microbiological aspects. The role includes: • Support for the department and laboratory employees. • Performing tests and working in a wet and accurate environment. • Update work procedures. • Work in a young and dynamic environment. Requirements • Undergraduate studies and above in the fields of life sciences, microbiology, biology, immunology and the like. • The balance of studies of at least two years - mandatory. • Availability for2-3 working days between 10:00-19:00 to apply for a job © Niloosoft 2026",
  "a13830f158fb4f42b75958a4fe0616c6c68fc972afc277284767e1cb8eab6e9e": "Sample/Sample in the Environmental Monitoring Team - Microbiology Description Sample/Sample in the Environmental Monitoring Team - Microbiology Integration into the QC Microbiology Group which includes the Microbiology Laboratory, Environmental Monitoring Team. The group is responsible for performing tests of the company's products during the various life cycle stages including environmental monitoring tests throughout the production area. Practice essence - Execution, reporting and approval of environmental monitoring tests according to procedures using the required equipment. Responsibilities and main tasks - Environmental monitoring tests (EM) in the production areas and their approval. • Updating procedures and documents relevant to the EM field, involvement in the certification of production facilities. • The work environment - clean rooms and a microbiology laboratory. • Strict work according to procedures and reliable results reporting according to work plans and schedule. Education requirements – Bachelor's degree practical engineer/engineer and above in the fields of molecular biology, life sciences, biotechnology and the like. • Skills – responsibility, professionalism, accuracy in details and technical performance, ability to read procedures in English, reliability, teamwork, human relations, initiative, ability to cope with stress and problem solving. • Experience working in a clean room under GMP conditions - advantage. Apply for a job © Niloosoft 2026",
  "0f01382696e74b5c95ab7e722696edabf147036519115cf2878c6599584e636b": "QA Associate- Quality Assurance Referent Description The team is responsible for setting the plant quality policy on various topics: environmental monitoring, clothing, documentation, quality record management, irregularities, corrective and preventive actions, internal inspections, proper behavior in clean rooms, performing QA Oversight on the factory departments (production and QC), participation in projects, investigations, and audits of regulatory bodies and customers. Job Description • The role includes accompanying and handling deviations and corrective and preventive actions (CAPA). • Review and approve batch bags • Writing and approving procedures • Conducting internal audits at the company • Execution of QA Oversight on the Production Department • Determining the quality policy on issues the team is responsible for • Participation in audits of regulatory bodies and customers • Participation as a QA representative in various forums Requirements • In-depth familiarity with the relevant standardization • Previous experience in QA in a pharmaceutical company - conducting investigations, implementing corrective actions, performing internal examinations, performing QA Oversight - mandatory. • Experience in writing quality policy documents • High level English • High oral and written expression • Education: Bachelor's degree or higher in life sciences/ biotechnology/chemistry/biochemistry/chemical engineering/pharmaceutical engineering/biomedical engineering/ pharmacy. The position is designed for both women and men to apply for the position © Niloosoft 2026",
